[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186133837 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-dcb73b7c-8cd5-5969-93ed-1bf898ab0795"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-dcb73b7c-8cd5-5969-93ed-1bf898ab0795" :question/id #uuid "dcb73b7c-8cd5-5969-93ed-1bf898ab0795" :question/math-academy-id "q-140491" :question/problem "Consider the **orthonormal** set $U$ below. By adding a new vector $x=[{x}_{1},\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}]^{T},$ extend the set so that it forms an **orthonormal** basis of ${R}^{3}.$ What is the value of $|{x}_{1}|+|{x}_{2}|+|{x}_{3}|?$\n\n$$\nU=\\{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $U$ as ${u}_{1},\\,{u}_{2}.$ To extend the given set to an orthonormal basis of ${R}^{3}$, we need to find a third vector $x$ such that $‖x‖=1,$ and\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot x=0 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot x=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}}{x}_{1}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{17}}{x}_{2}+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}}{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{x}_{1}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system above and reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{17}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=\\sqrt{17}\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{2}:=\\sqrt{2}\\cdot {R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}-{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=\\frac{4}{3}{x}_{3},$ and from the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}={x}_{3}.$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=3,$ we obtain the vector \n$x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nNow, we need to normalize $x.$ Notice that $‖x‖=\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{3}^{2}}=\\sqrt{34}.$ So, we normalize $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{‖x‖}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{34}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{34}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{34}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, an orthonormal basis of ${R}^{3}$ is\n\n$$\n\\{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{34}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{34}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{34}}\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $|{x}_{1}|+|{x}_{2}|+|{x}_{3}|=|\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{34}}|+|\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{34}}|+|\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{34}}|=\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{34}}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4e24f321-343d-593f-9ede-112a987e4533"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4e24f321-343d-593f-9ede-112a987e4533" :answer-field/id #uuid "4e24f321-343d-593f-9ede-112a987e4533" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c5abdd46-3123-599e-ba75-96985fec9ea2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c5abdd46-3123-599e-ba75-96985fec9ea2" "answer-07549629-124a-5c26-94d8-775576771467" "answer-530f1d3c-21d1-551b-a2d2-11e6d377597a" "answer-09a831bd-413d-5031-9d8f-47f63a86dc4c" "answer-293f3ef5-7bd8-58b9-8d4d-52c8d95cc564"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5abdd46-3123-599e-ba75-96985fec9ea2" :answer/id #uuid "c5abdd46-3123-599e-ba75-96985fec9ea2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{34}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07549629-124a-5c26-94d8-775576771467" :answer/id #uuid "07549629-124a-5c26-94d8-775576771467" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{34}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-530f1d3c-21d1-551b-a2d2-11e6d377597a" :answer/id #uuid "530f1d3c-21d1-551b-a2d2-11e6d377597a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{34}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09a831bd-413d-5031-9d8f-47f63a86dc4c" :answer/id #uuid "09a831bd-413d-5031-9d8f-47f63a86dc4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{34}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-293f3ef5-7bd8-58b9-8d4d-52c8d95cc564" :answer/id #uuid "293f3ef5-7bd8-58b9-8d4d-52c8d95cc564" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{34}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-31a4950c-e57e-5388-9d71-5baa611ca7b2" :activity/id #uuid "31a4950c-e57e-5388-9d71-5baa611ca7b2" :activity/title "Orthogonal Sets in Euclidean Spaces" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049811 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-e74678fc-cdaa-5c80-82f2-06de36ea9535" "step-7a87ebea-2c02-5322-b156-afea02e5b0a3" "step-34d88b52-a0d9-5edb-9036-074e82704885" "step-44855349-ccd7-57b0-9849-4398509b96fd" "step-f7d71d9d-b1d2-5a1f-a4ea-4a18a90b1556"] :activity/first-step "step-e74678fc-cdaa-5c80-82f2-06de36ea9535" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-e74678fc-cdaa-5c80-82f2-06de36ea9535" :step/id #uuid "e74678fc-cdaa-5c80-82f2-06de36ea9535" :step/content 17592186134220 :step/next "step-7a87ebea-2c02-5322-b156-afea02e5b0a3" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-7a87ebea-2c02-5322-b156-afea02e5b0a3" :step/id #uuid "7a87ebea-2c02-5322-b156-afea02e5b0a3" :step/content 17592186134283 :step/next "step-34d88b52-a0d9-5edb-9036-074e82704885" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-